# Dastro 3.4 — manual patch

Coding conventions moved out of the managed `AGENTS.md` block into a new
managed doc, `CODING_STANDARDS.md` (repo root). `AGENTS.md` is now an index
that points to it. Review tooling reads `CODING_STANDARDS.md` as the project's
documented standards.

## 1. Create `CODING_STANDARDS.md` if the upgrade did not

The upgrade that installs this version still runs the previous CLI, which does
not know the new doc. If the file is missing:

```sh
cp node_modules/dastro/consumer-docs/agents/CONSUMER-CODING-STANDARDS.md CODING_STANDARDS.md
```

Later upgrades keep the block between the `@dastro:managed` markers in sync.

## 2. Project already has its own `CODING_STANDARDS.md`

A file without the markers is left untouched, so the dastro standards are
missing from it, while `AGENTS.md`, `dastro-ai-linter.mdc` and
`dastro-create-modules.mdc` now rely on them. Append the managed block
(markers included) from
`node_modules/dastro/consumer-docs/agents/CONSUMER-CODING-STANDARDS.md` and
keep the project's own standards outside the markers. Where both state a rule,
keep one: delete the project's copy, or keep it outside the markers if it
differs on purpose.

## 3. Conventions kept outside the managed `AGENTS.md` block

The `## Conventions` section left `AGENTS.md`. Look for project copies of the
moved conventions:

```sh
grep -n "datocms.types\|dato:generate-types\|RSCSS\|rscss\|_font-types\|_ui-grid\|localePrefix\|localeLangTag\|boilerplate:init\|Conventional Commits\|isEmptyDocument" AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md
```

- A copy that says the same as `CODING_STANDARDS.md`: delete it.
- A project-specific rule about how code is written: move it into
  `CODING_STANDARDS.md`, outside the markers.
- Anything else (procedures, project facts) stays in `AGENTS.md`.

## 4. Custom rule files

`dastro-ai-linter.mdc` now lints against `CODING_STANDARDS.md` instead of
carrying its own rule. Project rule files that reference the linter rule for
the `isEmptyDocument` check should point at `CODING_STANDARDS.md`:

```sh
grep -rln "dastro-ai-linter" .cursor/rules
```

The reference docs `datocms-schema-changes.md` and `dev-server.md` are read
from `node_modules/dastro/consumer-docs/`. No action needed.
